The **Swedish MTBO Championships 2026** in Uppsala will feature a unique weekend concept. On Saturday, competitors will tackle **two MTBO races on the same day**, followed by a long distance race on Sunday.

A dual-race Saturday concept like this is quite uncommon in Sweden for MTBO events. Having seen this format work well in countries such as Portugal and Spain, we are excited to try it out in Uppsala and hope everyone will enjoy the experience.

We are working on a time schedule for Saturday so that everyone is going to have a good time in the forest, time to rest between the races, and time for the prize giving and the joyful dinner in the evening. It is a bit of a challenge, but we have found a very good setup for the weekend that we are happy with.

## Saturday Schedule & Venues

### Morning: Middle Distance

Saturday begins with the **Middle Distance** from the **OK Linné clubhouse**. It will be a fast-paced race with an extremely dense track and path network. It is going to be lots of fun and lots of orienteering.

![Middle Distance Map Sample](~/assets/images/posts/getready-mtbosm26/kartprov_medel.png)

### Afternoon: Sprint Distance (approx. 15:30)

After lunch, at approximately 15:30, we start with the **Sprint race**. We are very grateful to the **Swedish Agricultural University (SLU)** that we can use their area for having this competition.

We are going to experience a race in a university, botanical garden, park, and a little bit of forest. It is super exciting to have this race and see what it gives. We don't think we ever had an area like this before, so we will see how people handle it.

![Sprint Map Sample](~/assets/images/posts/getready-mtbosm26/kartprov_sprint.png)

### Important Rules for Championship Classes (H21, D21, H17-20, D17-20)

To create an exciting and fair competition for everyone, we have decided that participants in the SM classes (**H21, D21, H17-20, D17-20**) are not allowed to visit the arena at Syltahallen or its parking before their start.

Instead, you go directly to the start from the outside without passing the competition area. We provide a map showing the **Model Event area for warming up** as well as directions to the start. You simply arrive at the start when you wish, in time for your start time. After finishing, you are free to stay at the arena.

_Tip: Leave your car at OK Linné clubhouse and cycle to the sprint start, or send your luggage to the arena with company._

## Sunday: Long Distance

The **Long Distance** on Sunday will be demanding. We believe that many classes will have longer than expected winning times, but at the same time we believe that it is true long distance courses with the right character for long distance — an **endurance race** with orienteering navigation.

![Long Distance Map Sample](~/assets/images/posts/getready-mtbosm26/kartprov_lang.png)

## International Elite Field & Early Start Times

One extremely fun thing now is that we have lots of elite riders from many other countries coming to join us to practice and fine-tune for the upcoming World Championships that are taking place just a little more than a week after this race. We have riders from the **Czech Republic, Portugal and France** taking part in the competitions, and we are very happy for that.

To make a good race for everyone, we have decided to let the elite riders start first. The Swedish Championship classes (**H21, D21, H17-20, D17-20**) are going to start during the first hour every race. We believe that will mean the elite can race in the forest without having to look for all other participants at the same time, which we hope will be very beneficial and safe.

## Youth Swedish Championships (USM)

We also have the **Youth Swedish Championships (USM)**, where we see the future Swedish elite. We are very grateful that they are here to compete at our courses, so we will give them all the publicity that they deserve during this weekend.

We believe that is very important, and the USM should be as popular and prestigious for youth in that age group as going to the USM for runners are. We hope in a couple of years that will be something all orienteering youth will attend.

## Prize Giving, Dinner & Meals

At the sprint arena we will hold the prize giving for both Saturday races. We have two competitions in one: for participants representing a Swedish club and living in Sweden, you are competing for the Swedish Championships and the medals. All others are highly welcome to take part in our competition and compete for points in the Swedish Cup and the prizes offered for winning Swedish Cup races.

On Sunday, we will also crown the **total winner of the Swedish Cup** (best 4 results of 5 in the series).

- **Dinner:** We have organized the restaurant at the arena to be open for dinner. It is not a formal dinner, it is more like food for everyone. Please make sure to pre-book your dinner in Eventor or send us an email if you find that too hard.
- **Soup Lunch:** There is also a possibility to have a soup lunch that we also need pre-ordered so that we have the right amount.

